 # Upgrade PgFlow schema
 
-Use this for an existing installation when a dependency adds a core or helpers migration. PgFlow 0.4.0 aligned with upstream SHA `94490709f79ebf366141dd925b047f0c1013e759` at core V02 + helpers V05; do not call that published npm `0.17.0` compatibility. PgFlow 0.5.0 keeps core V02 and adds helpers V06.
+Use this for an existing installation when a dependency adds a core or helpers migration. PgFlow 0.6.0 targets upstream pgflow 0.17.2 (`baa9e43f5f9122133deacbc3e8ffc80e284b4f50`): core V03 and helpers V07. PgFlow 0.4.0 stayed on core V02 and helpers V05. PgFlow 0.5.0 stayed on core V02 and added helpers V06. Those earlier releases are not the current schema.
+
+## pgflow 0.6.0 stop-and-drain
+
+Anyone on core V02 and helpers V06 or earlier who will share the database with TypeScript 0.17.x workers follows this order:
+
+1. `mix pgflow.audit_slugs` must print no findings.
+2. Stop every Elixir worker and every TypeScript worker. Wait until `SELECT count(*) FROM pgflow.step_tasks WHERE status IN ('queued', 'started')` is 0, or accept that queued tasks resume after the upgrade.
+3. `mix pgflow.setup --upgrade`, then `mix ecto.migrate`. The generated file is `<timestamp>_upgrade_pgflow_core_v03_helpers_v07.exs`. It sets `lock_timeout` and fails the transaction on any slug finding. The migration never renames a slug.
+4. Deploy the Elixir release that requires core V03 and helpers V07, then TypeScript 0.17.x workers on flow-mode flows only.
+
+`down/0` is forward-only. Restore the backup taken before the outage.
+
+## Slug rules
+
+`pgflow.is_valid_slug/1` accepts only `[A-Za-z0-9_]`, must start with a letter, must end with a letter or digit, must not contain `__`, must be at most 128 characters, and must not be `run`. The flow-mode queue name is `lower(flow_slug)`, at most 47 characters, and unique across flows and jobs. Step slugs that differ only by case collide.
+
+Compile-time errors use the same reasons: `empty`, `too_long`, `bad_chars`, `bad_start`, `bad_end`, `double_underscore`, `reserved`, and `queue_name_too_long`. Rename the flow or step in Elixir code and redeploy. Do not edit the slug in SQL.
+
+## Step mode and routing
+
+Elixir refuses a step-mode flow at boot, before compilation, even when local recompilation is enabled. A TypeScript step-mode worker is a separate deployment and does not share the Elixir worker's queue. A queue-mode or route mismatch is `{:error, {:flow_routing_mismatch, message}}`. `message` is the upstream text.
+
+Workers stamp `workers.pgflow_version` as `elixir-<package version>` through the four-argument `register_worker`.
 
